<title>EGYPT: Egypt raises price of two cotton varieties - trade.</title>
<headline>Egypt raises price of two cotton varieties - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian exporters said on Monday they had raised prices for the Giza 77 and Giza 86 cotton variety on high international demand.</p>
<p>The Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association said it raised Giza 77 overall prices by one centilibre (one U.S. cent per lb) and Giza 86 by three centilibres. All prices are valid until 2200 GMT on November 2.</p>
<p>The association said prices for all other grades and varieties were unchanged.</p>
<p>Prices in centilibres (last week's prices in brackets)-</p>
<p>	   FG/EX   FG+1/4   FG	FG-1/4   G/FG   G+3/8   G+1/4</p>
<p>Giza 76  171.0   165.0    159.0   153.0    147.0  144.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 70  164.0   158.0    152.0   146.0    140.0  137.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 77  160.0   154.0    148.0   142.0    136.0  133.0    --</p>
<p>	  (159.0   153.0    147.0   141.0    135.0  132.0    --)</p>
<p>Giza 86  142.0   136.0    130.0   124.0    118.0  115.0    --</p>
<p>	  (139.0   133.0    127.0   121.0    115.0  112.0    --)</p>
<p>Giza 75  134.0   128.0    122.0   116.0    110.0  107.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 85  131.0   125.0    119.0   113.0    107.0  104.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 83  127.0   121.0    115.0   109.0    103.0  100.0    --</p>
<p>Giza 80  127.0   121.0    115.0   109.0    103.0  100.0    --</p>
<p>Note: FG/EX = fully good/excellent, G/FG = good/fully good</p>
<p>--Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/91</p>
